---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProjectNavigation from "../components/ProjectNavigation.astro";
import { appsBySlug, collection, companionApps, person } from "../data/site";

const projectHelp = [
  { title: appsBySlug.foodscanner.title, href: "#foodscanner", detail: "iPhone photo analysis and optional Google Glass setup." },
  { title: appsBySlug.glasshole.title, href: "#glasshole", detail: "iPhone sessions, AI providers and optional Google Glass setup." },
  { title: appsBySlug["streaming-devices-kids-meal-mode"].title, href: "/apps/streaming-devices-kids-meal-mode#compatibility", detail: "Fire TV / Android TV installation and streaming-app compatibility." },
  { title: "Local AI game experiment", href: "/apps/qwen38-27b-eval#play", detail: "Browser controls, playable game and source download." },
  { title: appsBySlug["book-cricket"].title, href: "/apps/book-cricket/support", detail: "In development. Preview the gameplay guide and nearby-match help." },
  { title: appsBySlug["ring-local"].title, href: "/apps/ring-local#validation", detail: "Project setup. No downloadable app or verified device connection yet." },
  { title: appsBySlug["strap-local"].title, href: "/apps/strap-local#validation", detail: "Project setup. No downloadable app or verified device connection yet." },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support"
  description="Help with Scaling Human apps and personal experiments: project guides, iPhone and Google Glass setup, compatibility and contact details."
  path="/support.html"
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="page-header__kicker">Help</p>
      <h1 class="page-header__title">Support</h1>
      <p class="page-header__lead">
        Help with the apps and personal experiments in the collection. Choose
        your project below, or email the project owner with a question.
      </p>
      <div class="page-header__actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={`mailto:${person.email}?subject=Scaling%20Human%20support`}>Email for help</a>
        <a href="/contact.html">Contact details</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <p class="updated">Last updated: October 11, 2026</p>

    <ProjectNavigation links={[
      { label: "Choose a project", href: "#project-help" },
      { label: "iPhone apps", href: "#iphone-apps" },
      { label: "Google Glass setup", href: "#glass-setup" },
      { label: "Send a question", href: "#request-help" },
    ]} />

    <h2 id="project-help">Choose your project</h2>
    <ul class="support-projects">
      {projectHelp.map((project) => (
        <li><a href={project.href}><strong>{project.title}</strong><span>{project.detail}</span></a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>The separate co-op utility has its own <a href="/apps/rt-library/support">RT Library support page</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="iphone-apps">Food Scanner and Glasshole on iPhone</h2>
    <p>
      Both apps require iOS 26.0 or later. You can use either app entirely from
      your iPhone; companion hardware is optional.
    </p>
    <p>
      Glasshole supports Apple Intelligence on compatible iPhone models. Other
      supported iPhones can use configured cloud, local-network, PocketPal, or
      custom providers. Food Scanner’s default Local iPhone Vision mode works on
      supported iPhones without an API key.
    </p>

    <h3 id="foodscanner">Food Scanner</h3>
    <p>
      Food Scanner can be used without companion hardware by choosing a food
      photo from iPhone or taking a new iPhone camera photo. The optional Google
      Glass XE companion APK can capture a food image and send it to the iOS app
      over local Wi-Fi or iPhone Personal Hotspot.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Glass, open the <strong>scan food</strong> command and
      <strong>tap</strong> the touchpad to launch and capture. Do not rely on
      saying “Ok Glass.”
    </p>
    <p>
      Nutrition values are AI estimates for general information only, not medical
      advice.
    </p>

    <h3 id="glasshole">Glasshole AI</h3>
    <p>
      Glasshole can be used without companion hardware by tapping the microphone
      button in the iOS app. The optional Google Glass XE companion APK can start
      and stop real-time conversation capture and display AI-powered fact-check
      overlays after analysis.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Glass, open the <strong>fact check</strong> command and
      <strong>tap</strong> the touchpad to launch, then tap again to start/stop
      listening. Do not rely on saying “Ok Glass.”
    </p>
    <p>
      Use Glasshole only with the consent of everyone being recorded and in
      compliance with local laws and regulations where you use it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="glass-setup">Optional Google Glass XE setup</h2>
    <p>Follow these steps only if you want to use a Google Glass XE companion. For standalone iPhone use, install the app and choose your processing mode.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Install <a href={appsBySlug.foodscanner.appStoreUrl}>Food Scanner</a> or <a href={appsBySlug.glasshole.appStoreUrl}>Glasshole AI</a> from the App Store.</li>
      <li>
        From the app page on this site (or the links below), download the
        matching companion APK:
        <a href={companionApps.foodscanner.apkUrl}>Food Scanner</a> or
        <a href={companionApps.glasshole.apkUrl}>Glasshole AI</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Follow the
        <a href={companionApps.foodscanner.guideUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Google Glass XE installation guide on GitHub</a
        >
        for ADB install, USB debugging, and hotspot setup.
      </li>
      <li>
        Connect Google Glass XE to your iPhone Personal Hotspot before opening
        the iPhone app.
      </li>
      <li>Open the iOS app and confirm the connection indicator.</li>
      <li>
        On Glass, <strong>tap</strong> the <strong>fact check</strong> or
        <strong>scan food</strong> command — do not depend on “Ok Glass” voice
        wake.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="request-help">Send a question or report a problem</h2>
    <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${person.email}?subject=Scaling%20Human%20support`}>{person.email}</a>. These are personal projects maintained by {person.name}. A useful report includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The app or project name and app version, if available.</li>
      <li>Your device model and operating-system version.</li>
      <li>What you expected, what happened, and the steps or error message that led to it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Leave out API keys, account credentials, private recordings and health data. A screenshot with personal information removed can help.</p>
    <p>You can also browse the <a href={collection.notes} rel="noopener noreferrer">project notes on GitHub</a> for scope, status and known limitations. Each project page links its own privacy and use information.</p>

    <div class="links-row">
      <a href="/privacy.html">Food Scanner &amp; Glasshole privacy</a>
      <a href="/apps/foodscanner">Food Scanner</a>
      <a href="/apps/glasshole">Glasshole AI</a>
      <a href="/#projects">All projects</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .updated { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .support-projects {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .support-projects li { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }

  .support-projects a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .support-projects a:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }

  .support-projects span { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.875rem; }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .support-projects { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
</style>
